Original commit body from 6264e65772532730ae44ff414a83a68033c29cc6:

Route markers took the literal path of `get`/`live`/`resources`, so
`scope "/admin"` + `get "/users"` was `/users`, and routes in different
scopes with the same tail collapsed under one label. The scope-aware walk
now carries path segments as well as the alias: a `scope` contributes its
positional or `path:` segments, and a `resources ... do` block nests its
routes under the member path `<path>/:<name>_<param>` (Phoenix.Naming
resource_name of the controller, `name:`/`param:` overrides; bare path for
a singleton). Paths are joined the way Phoenix's join_path does, so empty
and trailing segments vanish (`scope "/admin"` + `live "/"` is `/admin`).
Route-argument parsing is extracted into `_parse_route_args`, shared by the
extractor and the nested-resources scope.

On thc: 377 router markers, 359 -> 377 distinct names; `hypergumbo routes`
lists 371 -> 389 routes.

